CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ direct-list-initialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ from the prvalue: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ empty and non-empty bases: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Fixed: the braced explicit type conversion paired the elements with the
class's own members after skipping only EMPTY bases, so the clause of a
base with data members went to the first member (t.w = 6).  Such bases
now take the constructor path, which initializes the base subobject.
